.SH NAME
messq-completion-fish - emit the fish completion script


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmessq completion fish [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Emit the fish completion script for the messq command tree onto stdout.
Source it from your fish startup file; it wires the __complete protocol so
flags, commands and help topics finish on TAB. The script itself is static; the
live stream and consumer names it offers are fetched per keystroke on the
resolver's 200ms budget, and a dead daemon simply completes nothing, silently.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for fish


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--addr\fP="unix:///run/messq/messq.sock"
	daemon address (unix://, http://, https://)

.PP
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	colour: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--full-ids\fP[=false]
	print full ULIDs instead of abbreviated ones

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="auto"
	output mode: auto|table|json|ndjson

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress narration; data and errors unaffected

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	per-request deadline (0 = none)

.PP
\fB--token-file\fP=""
	file holding the bearer token, mode 0600

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	narrate (-vv dumps each HTTP exchange and the resolved config)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
